---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';

const houseFormat = [
  ['Recommendation', 'The call (Long/Short/Hold), conviction, price target, horizon.'],
  ['Executive Summary', 'The thesis in a paragraph: what I think, why, and why now.'],
  ['Company Overview', 'How the company operates and makes money.'],
  ['Industry & Competitive Positioning', 'The market structure and where the company stands within it.'],
  ['Investment Thesis & Variant View', 'Where my view differs from consensus or the price — with the reasons.'],
  ['Catalysts', 'The identifiable catalysts for the thesis to play out.'],
  ['Valuation', 'A DCF reconciled against comparable companies and precedent transactions.'],
  ['Financial Model Summary', 'Key drivers and outputs from the underlying three-statement model.'],
  ['Sensitivity & Scenario Analysis', 'How the target moves under bear / base / bull assumptions.'],
  ['Risks, Mitigants & Disconfirmers', 'The threats to the thesis, their mitigants, and the disconfirming evidence I’m watching for.'],
  ['Position & Sizing', 'How the idea translates into a position in the paper book, and why that size.'],
  ['Appendix & Sources', 'Primary filings, data, and the trail behind the numbers.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How Starzecki Research works — the 12-section report format, the paper portfolio, S&P 500 benchmarking, position sizing, and why losing calls stay published."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">Methodology</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      The value of research is in the reasoning and the record. This page explains exactly how both
      are produced here so you can judge the work on its merits.
    </p>

    <!-- Report format -->
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Anatomy of a report</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Every report follows the same 12 sections. Consistency makes the work easier to read and harder
      to fudge — the same questions get answered every time.
    </p>
    <ol class="mt-6 space-y-3">
      {
        houseFormat.map(([title, desc], i) => (
          <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-lg border border-line bg-card p-4">
            <span class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-accent tabular-nums">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{title}</p>
              <p class="mt-0.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <!-- Paper portfolio -->
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-2xl text-ink">The paper portfolio</h2>
    <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Ideas become positions in a hypothetical <strong class="text-ink">$100MM</strong> long/short
        book. It is <strong class="text-ink">paper</strong> — no real capital is deployed — and
        <strong class="text-ink"> price-only</strong>, marked to market without dividends, financing,
        or borrow costs. The goal is a clean, honest read on whether the calls add value.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each position is entered at the price on the publication date, so the entry can’t be
        cherry-picked after the fact. Positions stay marked until they’re explicitly closed, and the
        entry and closing prices are part of the permanent record.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Benchmarking -->
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Benchmarking vs the S&amp;P 500</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Net asset value is indexed to 100 at inception and tracked against the S&amp;P 500 over the same
      window. The number that matters is <strong class="text-ink">excess return</strong> — NAV minus
      the benchmark. Beating the market is the bar; matching it with more risk is not a win.
    </p>

    <!-- Sizing -->
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Position sizing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Size follows conviction and risk, not enthusiasm. Higher-conviction ideas with clearer
      catalysts and more downside protection get more weight; speculative or thinner-edge ideas are
      kept small. Every report states its size and the reasoning behind it.
    </p>

    <!-- Losers stay -->
    <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Losers stay published</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Nothing is deleted. Calls that go wrong remain on the site with their original timestamp and
      price, and closed positions stay in the record. A track record only means something if it
      includes the misses — so this one does, on purpose.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <Disclaimer variant="full" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
